/target
# A second target dir, used once to reproduce the default-target number in
# .cargo/config.toml — the one that shows what `-C target-cpu=native` is worth.
# Kept out of /target so the measured binaries are never a mix of the two.
/target-baseline
# CAP metadata is fetched, not vendored: tens of GB at full scale, and it is
# reproducible from tools/fetch_cap.py plus the snapshot date in the manifest.
/corpus
# Built indexes are derived artifacts. The manifest that describes one is
# committed; the multi-hundred-megabyte file it describes is not.
*.pirdb
tools/.nvrtc/
